title:: CaosTrack
summary:: 32-step pattern for one track (step model).
categories:: CaosBox
related:: Classes/CaosSequencer, Classes/CaosInstrument

description::
Each track (link::Classes/CaosBox#*tracks::) is a CaosTrack. The mode defines what
each step stores:

list::
## code::\snapshot::: stores the resolved value when the step is marked (percussion).
## code::\live::: stores only the gate and resolves the voice on trigger (melodic).
::

classmethods::

subsection:: Pattern generation

method:: randomIndices
Returns an array of step indices for a random gate pattern.
code::density:: is the probability (0..1) that each step is included. It is the
pure generator used by code::CaosBox.randPattern::; it does not modify a track.
code::
CaosTrack.randomIndices(32, 0.5);
::

subsection:: Solo state

method:: clearSolos
Drops every active solo. The environment calls it when it builds new tracks so a
fresh session never inherits the solos of the previous one.

instancemethods::

subsection:: API

method:: putStep
method:: put
method:: clear
method:: at
method:: step
code::
t = CaosTrack.new(\bass, \live, 32);
t.putStep(0, true);
t.putStep(4, true);
t.clear(4);
t.step(0);
::

method:: flam
Adds a flam to one or more percussion steps. Only valid for code::\snapshot::
tracks.
code::
t.flam(4);                    // amount 0.5, one extra hit
t.flam(4, 0.25, 2);           // two extra hits
t.flam([0, 4, 8], 0.5, 1);    // several steps
::
code::amount:: is the opening between hits (0..1) and code::repeats:: is the
number of extra hits (1..4). The hits are scheduled in tempo-relative time.

method:: removeFlam
Removes the flam from one or more steps.
code::
t.removeFlam(4);
t.removeFlam([0, 4, 8]);
::

method:: flamAt
Returns the flam event for a step, or code::nil::.
code::
t.flamAt(4); // (amount: 0.5, repeats: 1)
::

method:: onFlamChange
Callback code::{|track, index, value| ... }:: when a flam is added or removed;
the GUI uses it to redraw the step dot.

method:: muted
Read-only state set by code::CaosBox.mute::. A muted track keeps its pattern and
its melodic line advances, but it does not trigger or play percussion.
code::
CaosBox.mute(\kick, true);
CaosBox.mute(\kick, false);
::

method:: solo
Read-only state set by code::CaosBox.solo::. While at least one track is soloed,
only the soloed tracks are audible. Several solos can coexist and mute wins over
solo.
code::
CaosBox.solo(\bass, true);
CaosBox.solo(\bass, false);
::

method:: isAudible
The resolved state: not muted and either no solo is active or this track is one
of the solos. Code::CaosTrack.step:: uses it before triggering.

method:: snapshotPattern
Returns an event with copies of the complete gate and flam arrays
(code::steps:: and code::flams::). The index is the position in those fixed-size
arrays, so there is no separate order to remember.

method:: restorePattern
Restores a snapshot returned by code::snapshotPattern::. Both arrays are copied
back by position and the view is notified for every step and flam. A snapshot
from a different track size is rejected.

method:: setInstrument
method:: releaseInstrument
The first voice enters immediately; a replacement stays pending until the next
trigger (code::activatePending::).

method:: onChange
Callback code::{|track, index, value| ... }:: when a step changes; the GUI uses it
to redraw.
